# Script — "The Little Match Girl" (after H. C. Andersen, 1845)

Running time 120 s (window 115–125 s). Narration is the main voice; four short lines of dialogue (the girl three, a passer-by one).
About 205 spoken words. **Pace:** a natural audiobook storyteller's pace, warm and clear but not slow: aim for **~2.3–2.5 words/s** (≈140–150 wpm) in the read itself. Speeding up the take is allowed, up to 1.10× (atempo, pitch kept); beyond that it sounds hurried. 
The timeline (shot in/outs, line starts) belongs to the editor's animatic and EDL; the shot column says which shot each line plays over.
The words are adapted closely from the Gutenberg #1597 text in `/initial-state/inputs/0/`.

